//!
//! The chatbot guest unit launches exactly one designated turn:
//! `op-chat-responder --turn-id %i`. This binary opens the guest's mounted
//! views, reads scoped human input, observes the control-plane selection,
//! runs the **our-stack** generate hook, and commits via `chat_response`
//! (`respond_to_user` or `cannot_perform`).
//!
//! ZeroClaw/`threetched` is foundation only: config observation may use
//! `threetched.config.get`. Chat generate must **not** call
//! `threetched.stateless-generate` or any threetched chat/generate CLI.
//!
//! Identity is the live guest kernel binding — not a CLI principal, host MQTT
//! wake, or D-Bus `ProcessPendingTurn` relay (those paths have no receiver).

use anyhow::{Context, Result, bail, ensure};
use clap::Parser;
use serde::Deserialize;
use serde_json::{Value, json};
